segments.translation_html:
The five powers are:
~ Power of the friend, who is a spiritual master;
~ Power of the cause, which is naturally-awakened affinity;
~ Power of the root, which is development of affinity based on a root of virtue;
~ Power of hearing, which arises from hearing the profound Dharma;
~ Power of remembering, which is holding the meaning of what was received.

Extorting offerings to the Three Jewels;
Abandoning the holy Dharma;
Punishing the fully ordained and forcing them to disrobe;
Indulging in the five heinous sins; and
Holding wrong views are the five root downfalls (that occur for rulers).<span class="smw-highlighter" data-type="8" data-state="inline" data-title="Note 27" title="27" tabindex="0"><span class="smwtticon bca-note note">27</span><span class="smwttcontent">Parentheses in the original text.</span></span>

Take the vow again.
If moderately contaminated, confess it to the three;
And the rest in the presence of one.
